1
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:05,631
I thought my parents were gone,

2
00:00:05,756 --> 00:00:07,466
but then I found Nisha.

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:10,760
<i>Maybe our Mom and Dad
are still out there too.</i>

4
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:12,512
Hey, Uki! Hey, Lan.

5
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:14,389
- Oh. Hi, Jae!
- Hi, Jae!

6
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:16,307
Ooh! Daemin!

7
00:00:22,231 --> 00:00:24,565
Great job, squad.

8
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:26,693
Welcome to the order.

9
00:00:30,948 --> 00:00:32,448
<i>Fire.</i>

10
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:34,200
<i>Air.</i>

11
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:35,536
<i>Water.</i>

12
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:36,912
<i>Earth.</i>

13
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:40,332
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,</i>

14
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:42,542
<i>master of all four elements,</i>

15
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:45,045
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

16
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,671
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

17
00:00:46,672 --> 00:00:49,424
<i>the world built
the Seven Havens.</i>

18
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,510
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,</i>

19
00:00:51,635 --> 00:00:54,680
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

20
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:56,974
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again...</i>

21
00:00:57,391 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>But I believe,
they will save it.</i>

22
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:28,922
Ellora won't know this mill
is dry until morning.

23
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,808
How dare you!

24
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:43,687
You're depriving Ellora
of its oatmeal and congee!

25
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:45,689
Do you hate breakfast?

26
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:52,321
Hi, handsome.

27
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:55,157
Shame to bruise
that perfect jawline.

28
00:01:56,158 --> 00:01:57,409
What do you mean-- Oh!

29
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:05,792
Whoa!

30
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:30,149
Shame.

31
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,028
The brigade just sees you
as muscle, sister.

32
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:34,237
What a waste.

33
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:36,782
Pancha, hi-ya!

34
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,581
Sorry, Jae!

35
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:47,541
I thought I had
that dirty grain snatcher.

36
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,669
It's fine, Uki.

37
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:51,420
At least we stopped them
from taking everything.

38
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:53,674
Four raids
in the last three weeks.

39
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:55,633
Why steal so much?

40
00:02:55,634 --> 00:02:58,261
What do a few bandits need
with all that food?

41
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:01,098
I was wrong!

42
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,600
They love breakfast!

43
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:06,102
Those bandits must be stopped,

44
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:08,355
before they take something
we can't replace.

45
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:19,032
I...

46
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,992
Morning, Commander!

47
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:22,411
And morning, you two...

48
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:26,539
uh... cadets...
that I barely know.

49
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,166
Um, what are your names again?

50
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:34,296
I've dealt with tornadoes
less chaotic than these two.

51
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,716
I'm leaving them
with you today, Jae.

52
00:03:35,841 --> 00:03:37,300
- Whoopie!
- Who-whoa!

53
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:42,097
- Hey!
- Ugh!

54
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,390
Old sesame buns again?

55
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:46,768
Mmm... So stale and crunchy!

56
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:49,354
You two will assist Jae
with his tasks

57
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,939
and stay out of trouble.

58
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,064
- Yes, sir!
- Maybe!

59
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,567
I'm trusting all three of you.

60
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:56,027
Don't let me down.

61
00:03:59,406 --> 00:04:00,489
Wha-- I...

62
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:01,824
Come on.

63
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:04,244
You two should go easy
on the Commander.

64
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:07,664
He's carrying the brigade
on those broad shoulders.

65
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,125
Uh... Mm...

66
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:13,628
Then he should let us help.

67
00:04:13,754 --> 00:04:17,591
I'm training all day while Pavi
ransacks the haven records.

68
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:20,302
So, no leads
on your parents yet?

69
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:23,138
I looked through
all the people quizzes,

70
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,723
the tiny human papers,

71
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:26,766
the dead guy letters.

72
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,100
She means censuses,

73
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:30,102
birth records,
death certificates.

74
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:32,813
But there's nothing
about any family

75
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,273
that sounds like ours.

76
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:36,526
People can't just vanish...

77
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,028
can they?

78
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:40,822
At least we have mom's lullaby.

79
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,491
That's something, right?

80
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:04,095
Oh, hey!

81
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:05,763
It's the Terror Twins!

82
00:05:05,764 --> 00:05:08,099
You're Karthik's nieces, right?

83
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,141
Uh...

84
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:10,392
Yeah.

85
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:13,646
We're from the strange side
of the family.

86
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:15,857
Circus performers.

87
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:17,733
Oh, yeah. Reunions are tough.

88
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:20,403
So many lion-bear attacks.

89
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:21,780
Mm.

90
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:25,742
- Mr. Daemin! You know that song?
- Yeah.

91
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:28,036
I mean, I only know it
because Uki sings it

92
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,663
all the time in the barracks.

93
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,498
Oh, Uki. Can't carry a tune,

94
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:35,417
but loves music
almost as much as critters.

95
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,045
Where is Uki?

96
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:40,131
If she's sleeping through
morning drills again,

97
00:05:40,257 --> 00:05:41,757
I'm going to have words.

98
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,093
Stern ones. Come on, girls.

99
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,610
Also, you're late for training!

100
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:05,240
Dang, and I thought Pavi
was messy.

101
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:07,325
Uki must not be here,

102
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:10,619
which is good for her because
look at all these infractions!

103
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,706
The paperwork
will be a nightmare.

104
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:14,915
What are you both talking about?

105
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,960
This room is perfect!

106
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:19,588
Ah!

107
00:06:19,713 --> 00:06:23,340
Found this
under Uki's pillow.

108
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:26,051
Is she an artist?
Or is this just...

109
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,053
trash?

110
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:30,223
Portable sports?

111
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:32,559
Uki has terrible handwriting.

112
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:35,269
Portable sports?

113
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:38,356
Portable sports.

114
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,358
Hey, that's fun to say.

115
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,152
We'll clean up later.

116
00:06:43,153 --> 00:06:44,696
Finding Uki is the priority.

117
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,573
I may know where she is.

118
00:06:50,285 --> 00:06:53,580
Ha! I'd recognize
those kachori crumbs anywhere.

119
00:06:53,705 --> 00:06:56,498
Ew! How long
have those been there?

120
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,128
No more than 12 hours.

121
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,134
Back already? Oh!

122
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,761
Good morn, Pavi.

123
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:10,597
Rare to see you inside my shop

124
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:12,473
instead of lurking out back.

125
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:14,934
And your... sister?

126
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:16,686
I didn't know
there were two of you.

127
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:18,395
Yeah!

128
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:20,649
I guess I don't talk
about her much.

129
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:24,068
She's just jealous
'cause I'm the cooler twin.

130
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:26,237
Have some free samples.

131
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,115
What can I do for you?

132
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:32,243
We're looking for a friend.

133
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:34,495
She might have been here
this morning?

134
00:07:34,496 --> 00:07:37,832
Uki... would have been wearing
a brigade uniform.

135
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:40,584
Uki! Of course.

136
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:42,628
Came in for a big order
for her family.

137
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:43,964
Bitter melon spring rolls,

138
00:07:44,089 --> 00:07:46,048
then had to dash.

139
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:47,466
Is she in trouble?

140
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,469
Hopefully, Uki's just late
to work and nothing else.

141
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,555
I'm sure that rascal
is all right.

142
00:07:52,681 --> 00:07:55,557
The brigade has more
on their plate than tardiness.

143
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:58,520
You should be out there
catching these no good bandits!

144
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,438
We're doing our best.

145
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:02,314
In fact, Uki and I
were part of the squad

146
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,192
that nearly caught them
a couple weeks ago.

147
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,528
Oh, good to know.

148
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:09,989
I can barely put enough dough
together for a single bun.

149
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:12,950
These attacks are taking
a toll on me.

150
00:08:12,951 --> 00:08:15,870
We'll catch these thieves,
I promise.

151
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:17,746
If Uki comes by again,

152
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:19,374
will you send her
to the compound?

153
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:20,958
Of course!

154
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:24,587
You know I've got my eye out
for you hardworking benders.

155
00:08:24,713 --> 00:08:26,046
Here, take some spare

156
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:27,589
spring rolls for the road.

157
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:30,175
The bitter melon
is really bitter.

158
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:31,635
Just how I like it!

159
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:32,721
- Hey!
- Thanks, Agam!

160
00:08:32,846 --> 00:08:33,804
Thanks, Agam!

161
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,183
Let's try Uki's family's house.

162
00:08:39,184 --> 00:08:41,604
Maybe she forgot to tell me
it's her day off?

163
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:42,563
I don't know.

164
00:08:43,063 --> 00:08:45,775
Something smells fishy
about this whole situation.

165
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:51,823
Portable sports.
Port, port... Portable sports.

166
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:55,075
Portable sports. Porrr...
Portable sports.

167
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:56,410
Portable sports.

168
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:59,913
Okay, when we grill
Uki's family, let me start.

169
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,458
I'll get 'em talking.

170
00:09:01,583 --> 00:09:03,293
We're just gonna ask
if they've seen Uki.

171
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:06,504
Maybe Uki was walking home
with cursed spring rolls and...

172
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:09,174
Bam! A crazed
spider-bird attacked her.

173
00:09:09,299 --> 00:09:11,301
Or Uki's mixed up
in the dark underworld

174
00:09:11,426 --> 00:09:12,634
of sheep-pig jousting!

175
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:14,511
Maybe the whole family's
in on it!

176
00:09:14,512 --> 00:09:16,889
Uki's family are lovely people.

177
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:19,391
We aren't gonna make them panic
for no reason.

178
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,644
And we are not grilling anyone.

179
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:25,106
You catch more horse-flies
with sugar than vinegar.

180
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:27,275
Not as much as camodillo manure.

181
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,194
Flies love that stuff.

182
00:09:29,319 --> 00:09:30,278
Focus, Pavi!

183
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,071
We're the Avatars.

184
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:33,698
We need to be helping people.

185
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:36,034
And finding a missing bender,

186
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:38,243
which is exactly what Uki is,

187
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:39,621
would be a big help.

188
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:42,164
Hopefully, Uki is at her house

189
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:43,582
having some chai and snacks,

190
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,960
and this is all
a big misunderstanding.

191
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:49,923
You both are way
too soft for these hard streets.

192
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:52,967
Hey! I'm from these streets!

193
00:09:53,343 --> 00:09:55,804
Good for you!

194
00:09:56,888 --> 00:09:59,641
Porr...
Portable sports.

195
00:10:00,058 --> 00:10:02,434
Porrr-table sports.

196
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,854
Psst! Pavi, dial down the weird.

197
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:09,274
Jae! How could you stay away
for so long?

198
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,984
Come in, come in!

199
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:14,155
You caught us on stock day,
so we're a bit crowded.

200
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:17,032
It smells amazing
in here, Ahnah.

201
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:20,369
Everyone, you know Jae,
Uki's squad leader.

202
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:22,247
And these are...

203
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:23,831
Nisha! And Pavi.

204
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:25,624
Say welcome, everyone!

205
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,835
Welcome! Hi!

206
00:10:27,836 --> 00:10:28,794
Good morning!

207
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,295
Can I get you anything to eat?

208
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:32,090
We've got some
blubber tagine on.

209
00:10:32,215 --> 00:10:33,132
We're okay.

210
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:34,509
- Absolutely!
- No thanks.

211
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,386
I'll get you three bowls.

212
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:39,972
Has Uki stopped by today?

213
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:42,141
Nope.
She should be here any minute

214
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,685
with the spring rolls, though.

215
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:46,186
- But she already left the--
- Uh...

216
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:50,066
Did she mention
anything... suspicious?

217
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,484
Talk about any enemies?

218
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:54,361
What Nisha means is,

219
00:10:54,362 --> 00:10:57,031
has anything been
troubling Uki lately?

220
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:59,409
Uki was ranting
about being exhausted

221
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,536
from fighting off
the Faceless raids.

222
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,289
Seemed stressed
about Ellora's supplies.

223
00:11:04,706 --> 00:11:07,166
Hmm... Anything else?

224
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:08,918
Animal attacks!
Overdue library--

225
00:11:09,878 --> 00:11:11,462
Should we be worried?

226
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:13,548
She was supposed to be here
a while ago.

227
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:17,551
Hasn't the Bending Brigade
asked enough of my Uki?

228
00:11:17,552 --> 00:11:21,222
I bet she's taking
a deserved day off!

229
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,432
Since Uki was little,

230
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:25,185
she'd skip out of training

231
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:28,437
to play with the camodillos
in the barns.

232
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:34,027
Uh, actually, we're looking
for Uki because of a song.

233
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:37,864
She could help me and Nisha
find our parents.

234
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,324
Wanna listen?

235
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:47,707
Know it?

236
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:51,126
Nope, not that one. Sorry.

237
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:53,504
Sir, we just find want
to find Uki.

238
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:55,756
No one's seen her
since this morning.

239
00:11:55,757 --> 00:11:56,925
Really looks like a case

240
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,219
of a missing bender.

241
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:01,762
Wait, so now she's missing?

242
00:12:01,763 --> 00:12:02,972
I'm not sure...

243
00:12:03,348 --> 00:12:05,349
If she finally up and left,

244
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:06,935
I'm happy for her!

245
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,853
Toklo, don't say that!

246
00:12:09,312 --> 00:12:11,813
You know the backlash we'd get
if rumors started

247
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:13,024
that Uki was a...

248
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,983
brigade deserter.

249
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:17,278
Business is hard enough
as it is.

250
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:19,571
Grandpa Pops?

251
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:21,824
We're not trying
to get Uki in trouble.

252
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:25,161
We wanna find her
to make sure she's okay.

253
00:12:25,912 --> 00:12:27,746
I know better than most.

254
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,540
Family is important.

255
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,918
My Uki's an independent soul,

256
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:35,046
I bet she just needed a break.

257
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:38,340
How about you three
check her old room?

258
00:12:38,341 --> 00:12:41,636
I saw Uki leave a mess
of things last time she visited.

259
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:42,970
Thank you,

260
00:12:42,971 --> 00:12:45,348
maybe it'll give us an idea
where she went.

261
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:48,350
When you find my Uki,

262
00:12:48,351 --> 00:12:50,852
you make sure she's safe.

263
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:54,065
I promise I won't let you lose
your family too.

264
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,277
Ugh!

265
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,782
- Oh!
- When we find Uki,

266
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,909
we need to introduce her
to a broom.

267
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:07,119
I had a friend who was a broom.

268
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,913
Yeah, very pushy.

269
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:12,375
Was Uki packing to leave?

270
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,836
What was she running from?

271
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:17,338
Whoa! Uki was onto something!

272
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:20,383
Whoa!

273
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:22,468
This is a map of Ellora.

274
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,970
Maybe Uki gets lost easily.

275
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:27,807
The streets are twisty
and also turn-y.

276
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:30,017
Wait! I know these spots.

277
00:13:30,018 --> 00:13:32,311
These are where our squad
has served.

278
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:34,522
We put out a library fire here,

279
00:13:34,856 --> 00:13:36,441
delivered a baby here...

280
00:13:36,983 --> 00:13:39,444
Stopped a Faceless attack there!

281
00:13:39,569 --> 00:13:42,155
Por-por-portable sports.

282
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,740
- Por-por...
- Aw! Uki must be proud

283
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:46,491
- of the work we do!
- Portable sports!

284
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:49,703
Portable sports! Por-ta-ble...

285
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:50,954
Oh, man!

286
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,539
Now I'm doing it!

287
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,665
Wait.

288
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,710
Give me that scrap
from Uki's bunk.

289
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:59,881
Uki didn't write
"portable sports!"

290
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:01,673
It's "possible spots!"

291
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:03,634
Pavi, you're a weirdo genius!

292
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,636
Aw! Thanks!

293
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,476
The red spots mark all the raids

294
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:14,269
carried out by the Faceless!

295
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:16,188
This was our fight
two weeks ago!

296
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:17,314
That's it!

297
00:14:17,315 --> 00:14:18,940
Uki was tracking the Faceless

298
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:20,317
<i>while on duty.</i>

299
00:14:20,318 --> 00:14:21,736
<i>She must've noticed
some kind of pattern</i>

300
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,571
<i>and figured out
the possible spots they'd hit!</i>

301
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:25,864
<i>Oh, oh, oh!</i>

302
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,533
<i>What if Uki picked up
the Faceless' trail</i>

303
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:30,078
<i>outside Agam's shop
and followed them?</i>

304
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:33,205
Wait. There are
a couple red spots

305
00:14:33,206 --> 00:14:35,415
the Faceless haven't hit yet.

306
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:37,251
The camodillo barns...

307
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:38,961
And the Western Gate.

308
00:14:39,379 --> 00:14:40,922
I need you two to get Karthik.

309
00:14:41,047 --> 00:14:43,841
It looks like the Faceless are
gonna attack the Western Gate.

310
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:46,052
And I'm gonna stop them.

311
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,977
Hurry up
before more guards show up.

312
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:58,940
Did you feel something?

313
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:05,320
Jae!

314
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,781
Boy, am I glad to see you.

315
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:09,699
We've been
up here for ages!

316
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,952
I'm dying to use the bathroom!

317
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:14,704
You've been holding it?

318
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,541
- You haven't?
- Hey!

319
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:19,127
You're in the wrong place,
brigade boy.

320
00:15:19,252 --> 00:15:20,752
It doesn't make sense.

321
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:22,546
The gate secures Ellora, sure.

322
00:15:22,547 --> 00:15:23,881
But why the camodillo barn?

323
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:26,383
There's nothing to steal there
but stinky animals!

324
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:28,844
Camodillos are actually
really neat!

325
00:15:28,845 --> 00:15:31,763
They're super strong
and impossible to catch.

326
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,890
Once a camodillo
starts rolling downhill,

327
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:36,519
they're bananas fast.

328
00:15:36,978 --> 00:15:40,439
No, I don't have any, Geet.
It's an expression.

329
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,317
If the Faceless are stealing
loads of stuff from Ellora,

330
00:15:43,443 --> 00:15:45,193
they'd need a way
to carry everything.

331
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,403
- Right?
- Sure!

332
00:15:46,404 --> 00:15:48,364
Camodillos would be great
for that.

333
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:51,575
But you'd have to get them out
of Ellora somehow.

334
00:15:51,576 --> 00:15:52,952
That's why they're at the gate!

335
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:54,536
The gate isn't the target,

336
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:57,330
it's just the way to get
the actual target out of Ellora!

337
00:15:57,331 --> 00:15:59,541
Maybe that's what
Uki figured out!

338
00:15:59,542 --> 00:16:02,002
She knows loads
about camodillos!

339
00:16:02,003 --> 00:16:04,129
We've got to get to the barns
to help her!

340
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:06,215
Shouldn't we listen to Jae
and tell Karthik?

341
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,592
The brigade needs to know.

342
00:16:07,717 --> 00:16:09,135
There's no time!

343
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:11,553
This is how
we help Ellora, Karthik,

344
00:16:11,554 --> 00:16:13,513
and bring Uki back
to her family.

345
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,725
And find out more
about Mom's lullaby.

346
00:16:16,142 --> 00:16:17,143
Let's go.

347
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:41,417
The camodillos
are already gone!

348
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,710
Wait!

349
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:45,087
There's the herd!

350
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,302
They're moving too fast!

351
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:54,179
We've got to direct the herd.

352
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,681
Got it! Stay sneaky, okay?

353
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:57,849
Oh, fine!

354
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:59,684
Let's save these critters!

355
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:40,893
The gate! Jae hasn't closed it!

356
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:43,104
I knew he'd need our help!

357
00:17:45,982 --> 00:17:46,941
Huh?

358
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:53,114
Huh?

359
00:17:58,369 --> 00:17:59,787
Pavi, watch out!

360
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:06,127
Earthbending and airbending?

361
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,049
- You okay?
- Yeah!

362
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,676
But Jae isn't!

363
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,318
Why didn't you get Karthik?

364
00:18:30,443 --> 00:18:32,360
Why didn't you close the gate?

365
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:34,029
Don't be a frowny frog, Jae!

366
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:35,573
We're here to help.

367
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:46,834
The gate!

368
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:57,386
We're almost there!
Push harder!

369
00:19:04,477 --> 00:19:06,145
No! We're too late!

370
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:13,361
Uki!

371
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:15,070
We have to go save her!

372
00:19:29,794 --> 00:19:30,961
Uki...

373
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:39,844
Disobeying direct orders
from Jae.

374
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:41,680
Getting involved in a stampede.

375
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:42,931
Putting yourselves in danger...

376
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:44,517
- But, Karthik--
- We didn't do that.

377
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:47,268
You're confined
to the brigade compound.

378
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,604
Indefinitely!

379
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,522
We saved half the herd!

380
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:53,317
You bent in public, Nisha!

381
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:54,777
We were helping!

382
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:57,696
You can help by staying hidden!

383
00:19:57,697 --> 00:19:59,031
End of conversation.

384
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:02,534
You know him.

385
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:04,578
He's most angry
when he's worried.

386
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,955
But you did what I would do.

387
00:20:06,956 --> 00:20:08,040
Really?

388
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:09,207
Mm-hmm.

389
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:12,043
Jae!
Let's have a chat.

390
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:13,462
Your turn to be in trouble now.

391
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:16,132
At least
we're in trouble together.

392
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,591
Jae...

393
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,010
I've done you a disservice.

394
00:20:20,428 --> 00:20:22,137
You need more time
before you're ready

395
00:20:22,138 --> 00:20:23,471
to care for the girls alone.

396
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:25,974
Sir, please give me
another chance!

397
00:20:25,975 --> 00:20:29,269
I've really made a connection
with Pavi and Nisha.

398
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:31,981
This isn't a punishment.

399
00:20:32,523 --> 00:20:34,649
With the added stress
from Uki's kidnapping,

400
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,153
I'm giving you some support
from a more...

401
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:40,029
experienced White Lotus member.

402
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:42,074
Somebody you can learn from.

403
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:43,992
Daemin?

404
00:20:43,993 --> 00:20:46,078
You're in the White Lotus?

405
00:20:46,454 --> 00:20:47,705
You never said anything!

406
00:20:48,122 --> 00:20:51,499
Uh, yeah. Kinda the whole point
of a secret society.

407
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,794
Ha! This guy, what a riot!

408
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:56,172
Daemin will help you
teach the girls.

409
00:20:56,589 --> 00:20:57,840
Dismissed.

410
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,134
Who wants a piggyback ride

411
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:02,719
- to the cafeteria?
- Yeah!

412
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,388
Woo-hoo! New big brother!

413
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:05,931
Daemin?

414
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:11,479
Something about today
still makes me feel...

415
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:13,063
off.

416
00:21:15,775 --> 00:21:17,234
I failed Uki.

417
00:21:18,027 --> 00:21:21,280
How could I let that happen
to my partner?

418
00:21:22,323 --> 00:21:23,657
We'll get Uki back.

419
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:26,076
And we'll find Mom and Dad.

420
00:21:31,248 --> 00:21:33,167
Thanks, Datu.

421
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:35,711
Happy to help, Han.

422
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:45,554
Molin?

423
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:48,973
I saw it...

424
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,433
with my own eyes...

425
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:51,351
What did you see?

426
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:53,978
The Avatar...

